#speaker:???
this badger is pretty young, despite his cane and obvious limping when he moves around. Always happy to chitchat, he's a warm person.

* Hi, I'm the train conductor, what's your name?
Mykola Tymchenko, at your service. Don’t worry, I’m not one of those passengers who touches things he shouldn’t. Used to fix these beasts for a living. #speaker:Mykola
->Mykola
                                          ===Mykola===
*you worked on trains ?
All my life. My father too. Guess it runs in the oil, eh eh !  If something rattles or hisses, I’ll hear it before the gauge does, don't worry about it, chief.
**you sound proud of your work.
Damn right I am. Any mechanic that respect themself should take their work seriously.  People forget these machines carry lives, not just cargo.
->Mykola
*•	How are you feeling ?
Could be worse. My leg complains, but at least I can sit down for once.
->Mykola1
                                         ===Mykola1===

* old injury ?
Yeah. Fell off a maintenance platform a few years ago. The ground won. Doctors said it kept me out of the army. Me wife calls it good luck.
** does it hurt much ?
Only when it rains, when I walk and stand too much or when the brakes squeal too long.
->MykolaDouleur
** how do you call it then ?
He shrug. A miss step.
// [If lost 1 health] : he sitting down, keeping a frozen smile on his face to not worry anyone. I'm just tired, don't worry chief.
//[if lost 2 health] : he sitting down, looking down at a photograph in his wallet. I'm not well, chief. I'm afraid I won't make it to the end. He stay quiet for a bit. Can you do me a favor?
->MykolaDouleur
===MykolaDouleur===
* come on, your going to be ok, Mykola. I'll make sure of it. Ok ?
He laugh for a few seconds yeah right, we will see I guess.
->Mykola2
* no, don't do this to me, Mykola. Not the dying speech.
If I don't make it, go to my family. Tell them everything. At the back of this photograph is there adress. If I die, take it and go see them. Ok ?
->MykolaDerniereVolonte
===MykolaDerniereVolonte===
** of course, Mykola. I will.
    Thank you chief. He gently tap your arm.
***no I won't because your going to live, ok ?
He sigh I will try my best, but if I don't make it, I'm counting on you.
->Mykola2
                                        ===Mykola2===
* anything for you Mykola. Tell me.
If I don't make it, go to my family. Tell them everything. At the back of this photograph is there adress. If I die, take it and go see them. Ok ?
** of course, Mykola. I will.
    Thank you chief. He gently tap your arm.
    ->MykolaDerniereVolonte2
    
** no I won't because your going to live, ok ?
He sigh I will try my best, but if I don't make it, I'm counting on you.
->MykolaDerniereVolonte2
===MykolaDerniereVolonte2===
***•	where are you from ?
From a small workshop town south of Khoren. Smelled like gas, metal swarf and cabbage soup, but it was home.
->MykolaOrigine
===MykolaOrigine===
* wait you worked on the railroad fortresses of Khoren ?! I heard of these giant machines of war. That must have been something !
Yes I did. He sound really proud of himself. I worked on assembling the weel system, not an easy work for something weighting like eight fully loaded trains.
->MykolaOrigine
* it's in the northern steppes, if I recall. People have it bad, I heard.
You heard well, but not from us. We are not the complaining type, you see. Yes the work is hard and the pay is cheap, but we work like a big family. If only you could see the joyful atmosphere in the workshop!
** what happened?
A bomb is what happened. A gas one. We had to run leave quickly the town. SRUR soldiers were waiting in the wood. It was a slaughter. His joyful attitude change to a serious tone. If it wasn't for this damn leg, I would have headed for  Akhilla to join up with our army.
->MykolaFamille
** it sound like a lot of fun.
It was, yeah.
•	what's bringing you aboard my train ?
My family's waiting for me in the neutral zone. I stayed behind too long, thought I could earn a bit more for my girls.
->MykolaFamille
===MykolaFamille===
* your family is safe?
They could flee faster than me with the armoured trucks of our army. I on the other hand had the chance to play hide and seek for a few days with the raïshurians. Lot of fun.
->MykolaFamille2
* why kind of jobs did you do in the meantime?
Scrapping old engines, fixing what was left. People still need trains, even in hell
->MykolaFamille2
*	do you have any family?
Sure thing! He brings out his wallet, where a small worn photograph show Mykola with a woman and a young girl. My wife, Olena. tough as steel. And our little miracle, Sofiika. Five years old.
->MykolaFamille2
===MykolaFamille2===
* you must miss them.
Like a fish in the desert miss water. But they’re safe, and that’s all a man can ask for now.
->MykolaRaison
* do you have news from them ?
I received a few letters when I was still working. It was mostly me who sent letters. But the next time I hear from them, it will be from their own mouth. He smile happily just imagining it.
->MykolaRaison
===MykolaRaison===
*	what will you do once in the neutral zone?
I don't intend to really change anything in my life, just do it somewhere else. I'll find work easely. Mechanics are still needed, even where the guns don’t reach. And I could by a bike to Soffika and teach her how to ride it.
**	observe
Mykola’s overalls are patched but clean. His claws are dark with grease, and his movements are practiced — efficient without rush. His limp is noticeable, but he hides it with humor.  His eyes light up when talking about machines, dim slightly when war or family are mentioned.
He is a good man, loving of others.
->END

